      "textEn": "H-SB, Canto 11, Vol. 1, tdk editing                                                              302. When a foolish person\nbecomes accustomed to spending all his hard-earned money to increase the prestige of his body and family,\nhe does not see how death is approaching his body and his\nfamily and friends' mortal bodies with a firm gait. Death is the destroyer of all—Lord Almighty\nDeath appears in the form of, which destroys all material things. In fact, even in the family,\none should use their wealth only for the spiritual upliftment of themselves and their family.\nIn the Krishna consciousness movement, there are many religious householders who lead a simple and peaceful life, and\nuse their wealth to carry out Krishna consciousness-oriented activities in their homes and to help those detached celibates\nand renunciates, who are engaged in propagating Krishna consciousness in public places. Even such householders who do not dedicate their hundred percent of power to Krishna consciousness,\nbegin to understand the spiritual principles of life properly and eventually become firmly spiritual at the feet of Krishna. In this way, they free themselves from these worries of birth, old age, disease, and death—bound. Without Krishna consciousness, life is essentially impoverished, but the impoverished materialistic person, whose\nintellect is limited, does not understand that true wealth is to elevate Krishna consciousness or divine love to the highest peak.\nSuch people raise their children like animals,\nwhose only purpose is false prestige and material sensual pleasure. Such materialistic householders\nkeep fearing that their children's ambition to gain false prestige by being more interested in spiritual life\nmay not be harmed. In reality, death will destroy all the efforts and plans of materialists who are devoid of such spirituality. If family life and wealth\nare used in Krishna consciousness, then man will learn to differentiate between eternal and non-eternal, soul and matter, happiness and sorrow,\nand in this way, the soul will be liberated and, rising above theoretical knowledge,\nwill attain the supreme accomplishment of a life imbued with Krishna consciousness. Limited sensory knowledge, that is, direct knowledge"
